+# TB-FIN-01C / TB-08-R2-R5-R5 — dedicated approval desktop and snapshot protection
+
+Parent: `867e58a87fd0a27aeea693739646b36edfa7f113` (tree `87c5f6da6768efb64858d7889e18d4b2b0ea66cf`). PAPER only. Local candidate; no main merge, live authorization or real desk changes.
+
+## Deployment contract
+
+The desktop entry starts only the fixed review service; it does not accept commands, credentials, display identifiers or approval payloads from the caller. The service runs under the existing independent `maj-vaj-approval` account and recovery group, with no network, no capabilities, narrow write access and no desk/native-private access. The exact polkit rule permits only the active local approval account to start the named unit. This is not an invitation to give normal desk users access to the approval account.
+
+Deployment requires an administrator-provisioned dedicated local X11 seat with logind reporting exactly one active, unlocked, nonremote user session for that account, a local display and seat, and an owner-only private Xauthority cookie in `/run/maj-vaj-review-display/Xauthority`. Provision the X server with TCP listening disabled, no broad `xhost` grants, and exclusive authorization for the review account. Do not copy that cookie into the normal desk session. Confirm the display is genuinely isolated. Install the fixed desktop entry, polkit rule and service only after that review; the separate root-owned `/etc/maj-vaj/review-desktop-enabled` marker is an explicit opt-in, in addition to the existing reviewed-recovery marker. Do not enable a timer or automatic approval. Session and cookie identity are rechecked before confirmation and publication. Missing/ambiguous/locked/remote/Wayland sessions refuse. This candidate does not provision the seat itself; positive operator desktop acceptance remains mandatory.
+
+## Protection routing
+
+Both native workers narrowly distinguish missing snapshot file and typed signed-replay freshness/checkpoint races from missing witness/pin, malformed or unauthenticated data. Only the ordinary snapshot-availability cases route to the existing independent protected reduce-only mechanism; no new order authorization or stale accounting authority is created. Existing entry lease/permit, snapshot freshness and watchdog settings are unchanged. Invalid or missing trust material remains fail-closed. The existing signed terminal settlement path remains authoritative.
+
+## Local exact-source qualification
+
+Pinned Python 3.12.16 and Freqtrade 2026.10 were restored from the shared offline packages; dependency check passed. Full suite: 500 discovered, 498 passed, 2 optional skipped, zero failures. Twelve new focused checks are included in that count. Actual separate-UID controlled-book PAPER native tests (8 checkpoints each): logical-clock signed snapshot expiry and real independent authority checkpoint advancement. Both retain the same native driver; existing exposure is reduced using its accepted grant, new entry/replay denied, accounting stays reserved until fresh authenticated evidence, and exactly one terminal settlement and acknowledgement complete. No public market, real credentials or real funds. The tests use disposable isolated ledgers and simulated time for expiry, not installed service wall-clock expiry.
+
+Initial host runs refused an unprotected source ancestry and encountered a Tk teardown issue in the unpinned environment. Corrected qualification placement and isolated the GUI test in a subprocess; no production trust check was relaxed. Final pinned rerun passed.
+
+## Offline Debian guest attempt
+
+Real systemd PID 1, loopback-only network, pinned runtime, 209/209 code and deployment file hashes. Installed the new review service definition in this disposable guest; `systemd-analyze verify` exit 0 and missing opt-in conditions correctly left it inactive with no PID. No genuine local X11 approval seat was provisioned; no positive production GUI or polkit activation acceptance claimed. The expiry cross-UID harness run under a transient systemd unit verified the signed wallet and then failed its existing 20-second warm-runtime readiness test deadline (unit exit 1); the checkpoint harness verified the signed wallet and was deliberately stopped before completion. These are not the installed named production-service lifecycle tests. No production deadlines were widened. Guest stopped cleanly, child image checks passed and original base SHA-256 remained unchanged. Complete actual named-service in-flight expiry/checkpoint change and real approval-seat interaction on a suitable native/KVM host before accepting R5-R5.
